    "A failed missing-catalog download resumes under the same job/intent when real content arrives; the failed protocol Task remains an immutable terminal snapshot, and a separate failed job cancels without publishing a destination",
    "Zero-byte binary input contributes exactly one canonical empty chunk and independently downloads to a verified zero-byte native file",
    "Independent official SDK Tasks stream: persisted intent, actual verification job, terminal result passes discovered output schema",
    "Native durable jobs have readable schema-backed resources and filtered templates; foreign principal resources fail closed",
    "Modern input-required retry preserves one real native interaction; forged JSON approval and foreign requestState cannot grant capture",
    "Modern Tasks use an explicitly negotiated per-request profile and actual canonical verification; omitted profile and foreign token are rejected"
